        {
          "headline": "SOCRadar says access broker CyberXero ran up to 51 Claude Code agents and holds 628,000 Ukrainian records",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "SOCRadar", "url": "https://socradar.io/blog/cyberxero-ai-iab-ukraine-critical-infrastructure/" },
            { "name": "The Hacker News", "url": "https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/cyberxero-uses-claude-code-in-campaign.html" },
            { "name": "Security Affairs", "url": "https://securityaffairs.com/200803/cyber-crime/cyberxero-used-51-ai-agents-to-steal-628000-ukrainian-records.html" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "SOCRadar's Threat Research Unit says CyberXero, a Russian-speaking, financially motivated initial access broker, runs \"up to 51 specialized Claude Code agents on the primary workstation\" grouped into offensive roles including c2-operator, exploit-chainer, scada-attacker and lateral-movement, plus a separate PentAGI deployment wired into a Cobalt Strike Team Server through an AI provider API.",
